// c-data-map-06: #[native] together with #[parallel] or #[serial] on one
// expression is always refused.
//
// command: graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/c-data-map-06.gx
//
// expected: prints [2, 4, 6]; the map fuses (it does without #[parallel])
// and its depth-0 loop takes the forced grain, as design/parallel_eval.md
// §7 describes for a fork-control node over a fused child.
//
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): refused at the decorated map:
//   #[native] expression did not fully fuse to native code:
//     - fork control runs its child under flags of its own
//
// `#[parallel] let f = ..` moves #[parallel] onto the body (fork_on_body,
// graphix-compiler/src/node/compiler.rs:101), where it joins #[native];
// compile_inner (compiler.rs:194-195) then wraps the node in ForkControl
// under the same decorated spec, so the census dispatches #[native] on the
// wrapper, which never emits (fusion::effect_blocker). Refused the same
// way: `|xs| #[parallel] #[native] array::map(..)`, `#[native] #[parallel]
// ..`, `|x: i64| -> i64 #[serial] #[native] (x * 2 + 1)`. Accepted:
// `#[parallel] (#[native] array::map(xs, |x| x * 2))`.
#[parallel] let f = |xs: Array<i64>| -> Array<i64> #[native] array::map(xs, |x| x * 2);
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
f([1, 2, 3])
